{"summary":"Fix positional printf width and precision argument lookup.","explanation":"Positional star fields use the same 1-based indexes as the conversion argument. The width and precision lookups currently add 1, so `%2$*1$d` with arguments `5, 42` reads `42` as the width: the assertions expect `"   42"` and `"42   "`, but observe forty spaces followed by `42`. Likewise, `%2$.*1$d` reads `42` as the precision: the assertions expect `"00042"` and `"42"`, but observe forty zeros followed by `42`. The positional width and precision tests also report `width is not integer` and `precision is not integer`, consistent with reading the wrong argument. `%3$*1$.*2$d` expects `"  00042"` but observes forty zeros followed by `42`, showing the same incorrect precision lookup. Pass each parsed positional index directly to `get_arg`; when parsing overflows, map its `-1` sentinel to `max_value<int>()` so it reports a missing argument instead of being treated as automatic indexing. Passing index zero directly lets the existing lookup report `argument not found` for `*0$` and `.*0$`, without later producing an indexing-mode conflict.","edits":[{"path":"include/fmt/printf.h","old":"        int width_index = parse_nonnegative_int(it, end, -1);
        if (it != end && *it == '$') {
          ++it;
          specs.width = static_cast<int>(
              get_arg(width_index + 1).visit(detail::printf_width_handler(specs)));","new":"        int width_index = parse_nonnegative_int(it, end, -1);
        if (it != end && *it == '$') {
          ++it;
          if (width_index == -1) width_index = max_value<int>();
          specs.width = static_cast<int>(
              get_arg(width_index).visit(detail::printf_width_handler(specs)));"},{"path":"include/fmt/printf.h","old":"          int precision_index = parse_nonnegative_int(it, end, -1);
          if (it != end && *it == '$') {
            ++it;
            specs.precision = static_cast<int>(
                get_arg(precision_index + 1).visit(printf_precision_handler()));","new":"          int precision_index = parse_nonnegative_int(it, end, -1);
          if (it != end && *it == '$') {
            ++it;
            if (precision_index == -1) precision_index = max_value<int>();
            specs.precision = static_cast<int>(
                get_arg(precision_index).visit(printf_precision_handler()));"}]}
